invariant: INV-17
file: sha512.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: a host object's sha512_of returns without wiping the context it
  hashed in, so its dead frame keeps the state after the last block and
  the end of the input. No library source calls it today, and a caller
  that hashes a secret with it would rely on the wipe sha512_of_hw makes.
  The digest is still right, so no vector sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test
  paints the stack, makes one sha512_of call on sha512.c's first arm, and
  requires no word the call computed in the bytes it wrote.

--- old
    sha512_final(&s, out);
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    sha512_final(&s, out);
